cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use IVIMBench in your research, please cite this software and the open
  IVIM standardization benchmarks listed under `references`. Companion IVIM
  methodology manuscripts noted below are PRE-PUBLICATION (no publication DOI
  yet); any Zenodo DOIs in their notes refer to software archives rather than
  peer-reviewed journal articles.
title: "IVIMBench: Standardized digital reference phantoms, clinical acquisition schedules, and uncertainty calibration benchmarks for quantitative IVIM MRI"
abstract: >-
  IVIMBench is a unified, open-source Python evaluation suite for quantitative
  intravoxel incoherent motion (IVIM) diffusion MRI. It consolidates
  physiologically grounded organ parameter samplers and 2D/3D spatial Digital
  Reference Objects (DROs) with exact Rician and multi-coil non-central chi
  noise injection, standardized clinical b-value protocols (OSIPI TF2.4,
  TCGA-LIHC, ACRIN 6698), reference estimators (NLLS, Two-Step Segmented,
  heteroscedastic MLP), and distribution-free uncertainty calibration metrics
  including D*-tercile and SNR-stratified conditional coverage, Cramér-Rao
  lower bound (CRLB) efficiency ratios, and boundary-railing bootstrap
  diagnostics. All cohorts and phantoms are synthetic and PHI-free.
type: software
